Ordinary 64-bit arithmetic can produce the mismatched value: `DADDIU` preserves the 64-bit sum, so incrementing `0x7fffffff` yields `0x00000000_80000000`. That establishes reachability, but not a wrong architectural answer from `EXT`; the manual leaves that case UNPREDICTABLE. I also found deterministic handling of other unpredictable cases, supporting disposition (a).
